SUNY Williams and Butch Wilmore flew on Boeing Starliner in June 2024 for what was meant to be an eight-day trip. They returned on a dragon capsule after 286 days because of propulsion concerns on the original vehicle.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:15.480
NASA chose the switch to avoid returned risks. Dragon flew a long mission without any software or hardware adjustments. Data after landing showed the propulsion system performed as expected during reentry and recovery.

